## 3. Opened and typechecked

These files exist. `oodac check` returned OK. Role is from the source.

| Module | What the file does | Caps |
|--------|--------------------|------|
| `core/list.oo` | empty / first / last on `List[Int]` | none |
| `result.oo` | `Result[String, String]` helpers | none |
| `str.oo` | thin string wrappers | none |
| `option.oo` | optional-string helpers as `Result` | none |
| `byte.oo` | `type Byte = Int` plus clamp/range | none |
| `math.oo` | IEEE-754 double wrappers (`sin`/`sqrt`/…) | none |
| `core/crypto.oo` | sha256, hmac, AES-128-ECB hex | none |
| `sec/objcap_hmac.oo` | HMAC-SHA256 seal of a payload string | none |
| `os/fs.oo` | read/write/exists/size wrappers | `&FsCap` family |
| `os/process.oo` | spawn / wait / kill / exec | `&ProcessCap` |
| `os/net.oo` | http / tcp / udp / tls wrappers | `&NetCap` family |
| `fs/path.oo` | path join and helpers | none |
| `fs/stream.oo` | virtual fd + owned store, not a kernel fd | none |
| `text/regex_nfa.oo` | `a+`, `a|b`, `[ab]` class scan | none |
| `text/regex_dfa.oo` | `dfa_compile` / `dfa_simulate` | none |
| `encoding/hex.oo` | hex encode/decode | none |
| `encoding/base32.oo` | base32 encode/decode | none |
| `encoding/varint.oo` | zigzag / LEB128 | none |
| `math/tensor.oo` | flat `List[Int]` new/get/set | none |
| `markup/toml.oo` | one `key = value` line | none |
| `markup/yaml.oo` | one `key: value` line | none |
| `markup/xml.oo` | two exact demo strings only | none |
| `markup/json_schema.oo` | `{}` parse; `validate` always false | none |
| `archive/{tar,zip,gzip}.oo` | magic detect only. Not decompress. | none |

`List[Int]` only in `core/list.oo`. Empty first/last returns `Err("empty")`.
`Float` is IEEE-754 double. Not decimal.
Process spawn/wait/kill need `ProcessCap`. Kill of pid 0 is refused.
epoll / inotify / prctl stay residual `Err` under `SysCap`.

## 4. Prove files on disk (not re-run this turn)

180 `../fixtures/prove_prod_*.oo` files. They import 179 std modules.
Those fixtures are emit+gcc+run shaped. This turn did not run all 180.

Named fixtures that exist:
`fixtures/std_list_main.oo`, `std_result_main.oo`, `std_str_main.oo`,
`math_trig.oo`, `std_markup_main.oo`, `std_archive_main.oo`,
`open76_fd_stream.oo`, `open77_aes.oo`, `open78_base64.oo`,
`open79_regex_dfa.oo`. Scripts `oodac_pure_build.oo` and
`math_trig_smoke.oo` exist. `open78` names base64. Base64 check is OK.

## 5. Residual visible in source

- 16 files write `List[Float]`. Runtime has `OoIList` and `OoSList` only.
- 13 files use a `*_stub.oo` name.
- `hash/sha256.oo` forwards to `crypto_sha256_internal`. Real sha256 is `core/crypto.oo`.
- Generic `List[T]`, `Option[T]` constructors, and generic `Result[T,E]`
  payloads are not implemented here.
- Full XML / YAML / TOML / JSON Schema is not implemented here.
- tar / zip / gzip decompress is not implemented here.
- `os/gpu.oo` is GpuCap CPU/noop. Device shaders stay `Err`.
- `os/python.oo` returns `Err` until CPython is wired.

## 6. Security

Pure modules must not open files, sockets, or env on their own.
Effectful `os/*` wrappers take a leading cap.
